---
description: Prefer Array<T> over T[] in TypeScript types
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Array types

Write TypeScript array types as `Array<T>`, not `T[]`.

```ts
Promise<Array<SchoolYear>>
useState<Array<Class>>([])
const names: Array<string> = []
```

Keep `T[]` only where it is not a type annotation, such as empty array literals or tuple types.
